name: asciidraw
kind: cli
description: >
  A terminal program for drawing ASCII mockups with the mouse: boxes, ovals,
  lines, arrows and text as objects you can select, move, resize, copy and
  paste. Pages, a library of ready-made pieces, and export to Markdown, PNG
  and JPEG.
visibility: public
language: go
tags:
  - cli
  - tui
  - ascii
  - diagrams
  - mockups
  - wireframe
  - terminal
  - go
notes: |
  Single static binary built on tcell. Objects are the source of truth: each
  frame composes them onto a character grid that also records which object
  drew each cell, for hit testing. ^S writes YAML (styles stored by name),
  ^E writes Markdown, PNG and/or JPEG per the S settings (image.go draws
  cells with Go Mono and pixel line art; PNGs are paletted). L opens a
  library: builtin pieces embedded from library/*.adraw, custom ones from
  ~/.config/asciidraw/library. `asciidraw export` and `convert` run
  without a screen (cli.go). y/d/p/x and ^C/^X/^V copy, cut and paste,
  using the system clipboard: pbcopy, wl-copy/xclip/xsel, PowerShell, or
  OSC 52 over SSH (sysclip.go). Releases go through GoReleaser to GitHub
  Releases, a cask in wkoszek/homebrew-tap, and deb/rpm/apk/arch packages.
  The macOS binary is universal, signed with the Developer ID and notarized
  by scripts/macos-sign.sh (notarytool profile sense-notary). Scoop, winget
  and AUR are configured but publish only with PUBLISH_SCOOP, PUBLISH_WINGET
  and AUR_KEY set.
  BSD 2-Clause. Asks Ghostty for Shift+mouse via XTSHIFTESCAPE. Tests drive
  the app through a tcell simulation screen.
